  {
   "id": "rqyAn9WyCAAJ",
   "from": "Funes, Martín",
   "author": "7c01398e6af26c2e",
   "date": "2018-07-04T17:42:20Z",
   "subject": "Re: [distance-sampling] Line transects visited several times",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-size:12pt;color:#000000;font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif\" dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\">Hi, let´s say that your transects are all of equal length, for example 4 km each. For those that were surveyed twice you add 4+4 and enter 8 km in the length box and you list all your observations recorded durign both\r\n repetitions. For those transects surveyed only once you just enter 4 km and the correspondent records. Quite simple.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\">Best</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\">Martin Funes</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\">WCS Argentina<br>\r\n</p>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font style=\"font-size:11pt\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><b>De:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; en nombre de Gilles Saulas &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gilles...@orange.fr</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Enviado:</b> miércoles, 4 de julio de 2018 13:58<br>\r\n<b>Para:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Asunto:</b> [distance-sampling] Line transects visited several times</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:12pt;color:#000000;font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif\" dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:&#39;Calibri&#39;;color:#000000;font-size:12pt\">\r\n<div>Hello</div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<p style=\"line-height:normal;margin:0cm 0cm 0pt;background:white\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN\"><font color=\"#212121\">In a recent study ), we did 21 line transects twice. For each, how to indicate that it is 2 times the same line transect and not 2 different line transects ? I try to use the parameter “multiplier”\r\n but the analysis gives the same result (Distance v 7.1).</font></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"line-height:normal;margin:0cm 0cm 0pt;background:white\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN\"><font color=\"#212121\"></font></span> </p>\r\n<p style=\"line-height:normal;margin:0cm 0cm 0pt;background:white\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN\"><font color=\"#212121\">In fact, some line transects were done twice, others only once; so, how to do ?</font></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"line-height:normal;margin:0cm 0cm 0pt;background:white\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN\"><font color=\"#212121\"></font></span> </p>\r\n<p style=\"line-height:normal;margin:0cm 0cm 0pt;background:white\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN\"><font color=\"#212121\">Thank you in advance for your help.</font></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"line-height:normal;margin:0cm 0cm 0pt;background:white\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN\"><font color=\"#212121\"></font></span> </p>\r\n<p style=\"line-height:normal;margin:0cm 0cm 0pt;background:white\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN\">Best regards,</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"line-height:normal;margin:0cm 0cm 0pt;background:white\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN\">Gilles Saulas</span><span lang=\"EN-US\"></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"line-height:13pt;margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"></span> </p>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n<table style=\"border-top:1px solid #d3d4de\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width:55px;padding-t